  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of Energy obligated $6.1B in FY2027 to date across 441 awards, with an average award size of $13.8M and obligations down 88.9% year over year. The FY2027 total is a partial, fiscal year to date figure. Year-to-year context shows prior fiscal obligations of $41.2B in FY22, $44.6B in FY23, $46B in FY24, $48.5B in FY25, and $55.1B in FY26. Facilities Support Services is the single largest NAICS category so far in FY2027 to date at $3.5B. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences follows at $1.1B, supported by narrower R&D categories that together add hundreds of millions more. The top vendors are primarily national laboratory contractors and nuclear site operators, led by TRIAD NATIONAL SECURITY, LLC at $875M. The FY2027 to date picture reflects concentrated spending in facilities support and national security research functions, with a small number of large awards driving the department total.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What did the Department of Energy obligate in FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Energy obligated $6.1B in FY2027 to date across 441 awards, with an average award size of $13.8M. Obligations are down 88.9% year over year. Prior fiscal years were $41.2B in FY22, $44.6B in FY23, $46B in FY24, $48.5B in FY25, and $55.1B in FY26."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which categories and vendors received the most funding so far in FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "Facilities Support Services received $3.5B, the largest single category. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences received $1.1B, and related R&D NAICS entries add $628M and $154M. TRIAD NATIONAL SECURITY, LLC received $875M, followed by NATIONAL TECHNOLOGY & ENGINEERING SOLUTIONS OF SANDIA, LLC at $633M and LAWRENCE LIVERMORE NATIONAL SECURITY, LLC at $550M."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Department of Energy spend on contracts?",
      "a": "The Department of Energy obligated $6.1B in FY2027 to date. The department recorded 441 awards with an average award size of $13.8M, and obligations are down 88.9% year over year compared with prior fiscal totals such as $55.1B in FY26."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Energy buy?",
      "a": "Energy buys a mix led by Facilities Support Services and R&D. Facilities Support Services received $3.5B, Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences received $1.1B, Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) received $628M, and Remediation Services received $290M, with other categories including Hazardous Waste Treatment and Disposal at $117M and Computer Systems Design Services at $21.9M."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are Energy's largest contractors?",
      "a": "TRIAD NATIONAL SECURITY, LLC; NATIONAL TECHNOLOGY & ENGINEERING SOLUTIONS OF SANDIA, LLC; and LAWRENCE LIVERMORE NATIONAL SECURITY, LLC are the largest contractors by obligations. TRIAD NATIONAL SECURITY, LLC received $875M, NATIONAL TECHNOLOGY & ENGINEERING SOLUTIONS OF SANDIA, LLC received $633M, and LAWRENCE LIVERMORE NATIONAL SECURITY, LLC received $550M."
